{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:15557131 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:15557131 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"15557131","source":"MED","pmid":"15557131","doi":"10.1164/rccm.200406-808oc","title":"Hydrocortisone infusion for severe community-acquired pneumonia: a preliminary randomized study.","authorString":"Confalonieri M, Urbino R, Potena A, Piattella M, Parigi P, Puccio G, Della Porta R, Giorgio C, Blasi F, Umberger R, Meduri GU.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Confalonieri M","lastName":"Confalonieri","firstName":"Marco","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4791-768X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Trieste, Strada di Fiume 447, 34100 Trieste, Italy. marco.confalonieri@aots.sanita.fvg.it"}]}},{"fullName":"Urbino R","lastName":"Urbino","firstName":"Rosario","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Potena A","lastName":"Potena","firstName":"Alfredo","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Piattella M","lastName":"Piattella","firstName":"Marco","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Parigi P","lastName":"Parigi","firstName":"Piercarlo","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Puccio G","lastName":"Puccio","firstName":"Giacomo","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Della Porta R","lastName":"Della Porta","firstName":"Rossana","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Giorgio C","lastName":"Giorgio","firstName":"Carbone","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Blasi F","lastName":"Blasi","firstName":"Francesco","initials":"F","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2285-9970"}},{"fullName":"Umberger R","lastName":"Umberger","firstName":"Reba","initials":"R","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4722-4031"}},{"fullName":"Meduri GU","lastName":"Meduri","firstName":"G Umberto","initials":"GU"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2285-9970"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4722-4031"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4791-768X"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["plain_english","recommended_reviews"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"171","journalIssueId":1216557,"dateOfPublication":"2005 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2005,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Am J Respir Crit Care Med","title":"American journal of respiratory and critical care medicine","essn":"1535-4970","issn":"1073-449X","nlmid":"9421642","isoabbreviation":"Am J Respir Crit Care Med"},"printPublicationDate":"2005-02-01"},"pubYear":"2005","pageInfo":"242-248","abstractText":"We hypothesize that hydrocortisone infusion in severe community-acquired pneumonia attenuates systemic inflammation and leads to earlier resolution of pneumonia and a reduction in sepsis-related complications. In a multicenter trial, patients admitted to the Intensive Care Unit (ICU) with severe community-acquired pneumonia received protocol-guided antibiotic treatment and were randomly assigned to hydrocortisone infusion or placebo. Hydrocortisone was given as an intravenous 200-mg bolus followed by infusion at a rate of 10 mg/hour for 7 days. Primary end-points of the study were improvement in Pa(O(2)):FI(O(2)) (Pa(O(2)):FI(O(2)) > 300 or >/= 100 increase from study entry) and multiple organ dysfunction syndrome (MODS) score by Study Day 8 and reduction in delayed septic shock. Forty-six patients entered the study. At study entry, the hydrocortisone group had lower Pa(O(2)):FI(O(2)), and higher chest radiograph score and C-reactive protein level. By Study Day 8, treated patients had, compared with control subjects, a significant improvement in Pa(O(2)):FI(O(2)) (p = 0.002) and chest radiograph score (p < 0.0001), and a significant reduction in C-reactive protein levels (p = 0.01), MODS score (p = 0.003), and delayed septic shock (p = 0.001). Hydrocortisone treatment was associated with a significant reduction in length of hospital stay (p = 0.03) and mortality (p = 0.009).","affiliation":"Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Trieste, Strada di Fiume 447, 34100 Trieste, Italy. marco.confalonieri@aots.sanita.fvg.it","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Clinical Trial","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Multicenter Study","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Community-Acquired Infections","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Shock, Septic","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CL","qualifierName":"classification"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pneumonia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Multiple Organ Failure","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CL","qualifierName":"classification"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Oxygen","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"BL","qualifierName":"blood"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Hydrocortisone","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AD","qualifierName":"administration & dosage"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"C-Reactive Protein","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AN","qualifierName":"analysis"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Anti-Inflammatory Agents","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AD","qualifierName":"administration & dosage"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}